  {
   "xml_index": 4,
   "xml_name": "L02_004_Price After Tax",
   "display_name": "Price After Tax",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Not all numbers are whole numbers! A <b>float</b> is Python's type for numbers with a decimal point, like <code>3.14</code> or <code>99.5</code>. Just as <code>int()</code> converts text into a whole number, <code>float()</code> converts text into a decimal number.</p>\n<pre>price = float(input())\nprint(price)</pre>\n<p>If the user types <code>50.0</code>, this reads it as the decimal number <code>50.0</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read the price of an item (a decimal number) and print the final price after adding 5% tax. The formula is:</p>\n<pre>final price = price + (price * 5 / 100)</pre>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>100.0</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>105.0</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
