  {
   "xml_index": 5,
   "xml_name": "L02_005_Circle Circumference",
   "display_name": "Circle Circumference",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's use the <strong>float</strong> type for another classic geometry problem: finding the <strong>circumference</strong> (the distance around the edge) of a circle.</p>\n<p>The formula for circumference, given radius <code>r</code>, is:</p>\n<pre>circumference = 2 * 3.14 * r</pre>\n<p><strong>Your task:</strong> Read the radius of a circle as a decimal number (use <code>float(input())</code>) and print its circumference using the formula above. Round your answer to two decimal places before printing, using <code>round(circumference,2)</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>5.0</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>31.4</pre>\n<p>(because 2 * 3.14 * 5.0 = 31.4)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
