  {
   "xml_index": 7,
   "xml_name": "L02_007_Concatenate Two Names",
   "display_name": "Concatenate Two Names",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>We just saw that <code>+</code> joins two strings together. Let's use this to build a full name out of a first name and a last name!</p>\n<pre>first = input()\nlast = input()\nfull_name = first + \" \" + last\nprint(full_name)</pre>\n<p>Notice we add <code>\" \"</code> (a single space, in quotes) between the two names, otherwise they would be joined with no space at all, like <code>JohnSmith</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a first name and a last name (one per line). Concatenate them using <code>+</code>, with a single space in between, and print the full name.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>John\nSmith</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>John Smith</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
