  {
   "xml_index": 8,
   "xml_name": "L02_008_Name And Age Sentence",
   "display_name": "Name And Age Sentence",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Here's a tricky but very common situation: what if we want to join a <b>string</b> and a <b>number</b> together using <code>+</code>?</p>\n<p>Python will NOT let you directly add a string and an int with <code>+</code> - it will give an error! You must first convert the number into a string using <code>str()</code>.</p>\n<pre>name = input()\nage = int(input())\nsentence = name + \" is \" + str(age) + \" years old\"\nprint(sentence)</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>str(age)</code> converts the whole number stored in <code>age</code> into a string, so it can be joined with the other pieces of text using <code>+</code>.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a name (text) and then an age (a whole number), one per line. Print a sentence in the exact format: <code>&lt;name&gt; is &lt;age&gt; years old</code></p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>Alice\n20</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>Alice is 20 years old</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "Alice\n20",
     "expected": "Alice is 20 years old",
