  {
   "xml_index": 13,
   "xml_name": "L02_013_Larger Of Two Numbers",
   "display_name": "Larger Of Two Numbers",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>So far, our conditions have compared a variable to a fixed number, like <code>n &gt; 0</code> or <code>marks &gt;= 40</code>. But we can just as easily compare <b>two variables</b> to each other!</p>\n<pre>a = int(input())\nb = int(input())\nif a > b:\n    print(a)\nelse:\n    print(b)</pre>\n<p><b>Let's trace through a few examples:</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>a = 8, b = 3</code>: <code>8 &gt; 3</code> is True, so we print <code>a</code>, which is <code>8</code>.</li>\n<li><code>a = 3, b = 8</code>: <code>3 &gt; 8</code> is False, so we print <code>b</code>, which is <code>8</code>.</li>\n<li><code>a = 5, b = 5</code>: <code>5 &gt; 5</code> is False (a number is never strictly greater than itself!), so we fall into the <code>else</code> branch and print <code>b</code>, which is <code>5</code>. This is still correct, since <code>a</code> and <code>b</code> are equal anyway - it doesn't matter which one we print!</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This same two-variable comparison pattern is everywhere in real programs - for example, picking the cheaper of two prices:</p>\n<pre>price1 = 250\nprice2 = 180\nif price1 < price2:\n    print(price1)\nelse:\n    print(price2)</pre>\n<p>Here we use <code>&lt;</code> instead of <code>&gt;</code> because we want the <b>smaller</b> value this time - always think about which direction of comparison your problem actually needs!</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read two whole numbers (one per line) and print the larger of the two. If they are equal, print either one (they're the same value anyway).</p>\n<p><b>Example 1:</b></p>\n<p>Input: <pre>8\n3</pre> Output: <pre>8</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 2:</b></p>\n<p>Input: <pre>3\n8</pre> Output: <pre>8</pre></p>\n<p><b>Example 3 (edge case - equal numbers):</b></p>\n<p>Input: <pre>5\n5</pre> Output: <pre>5</pre></p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "8\n3",
     "expected": "8",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": true,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "3\n8",
     "expected": "8",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    },
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "5\n5",
     "expected": "5",
     "extra": "",
     "show": true,
     "example": false,
     "in_precheck": false,
     "in_check": true
    }
   ]
