  {
   "xml_index": 16,
   "xml_name": "L02_016_Sum Of First N Numbers",
   "display_name": "Sum Of First N Numbers",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Loops become really useful when we combine them with an <b>accumulator</b> variable - a variable that keeps a running total as the loop repeats.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\ntotal = 0\ni = 1\nwhile i <= n:\n    total = total + i\n    i = i + 1\nprint(total)</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>total</code> starts at 0. Every time through the loop, we add the current value of <code>i</code> into <code>total</code>. By the time the loop finishes, <code>total</code> holds the sum of every number the loop visited!</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop and an accumulator variable, compute and print the sum of all whole numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive).</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>5</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>15</pre>\n<p>(because 1+2+3+4+5 = 15)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
   "mark": 1.0,
   "tests": [
    {
     "testcode": "",
     "stdin": "5",
     "expected": "15",
     "extra": "",
