  {
   "xml_index": 17,
   "xml_name": "L02_017_Countdown From N",
   "display_name": "Countdown From N",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Counters don't always have to count upward! We can also make a counter <b>decrease</b> on every repeat, to count downward instead.</p>\n<pre>i = n\nwhile i >= 1:\n    print(i)\n    i = i - 1</pre>\n<p>Here, <code>i</code> starts at <code>n</code> and <b>decreases by 1</b> each time, and the loop keeps going as long as <code>i</code> is still at least 1.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop, print the numbers from <code>N</code> down to 1, each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>5</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>5\n4\n3\n2\n1</pre>",
   "answerpreload": "",
