  {
   "xml_index": 18,
   "xml_name": "L02_018_Even Numbers Up To N",
   "display_name": "Even Numbers Up To N",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Let's combine what you learned about <code>if</code> with what you just learned about <code>while</code> loops! We can put an <code>if</code> statement <b>inside</b> a loop, so that only some of the loop's repeats do something.</p>\n<pre>n = int(input())\ni = 1\nwhile i <= n:\n    if i % 2 == 0:\n        print(i)\n    i = i + 1</pre>\n<p>Notice the loop still runs from 1 up to <code>n</code> every time, but the <code>print(i)</code> line is now doubly indented - once for being inside the <code>while</code> loop, and again for being inside the <code>if</code>. This is why it only executes for the numbers where the condition <code>i % 2 == 0</code> is true.</p>\n<p><b>Your task:</b> Read a whole number <code>N</code>. Using a <code>while</code> loop combined with an <code>if</code>, print all the even numbers from 1 to <code>N</code> (inclusive), each on its own line.</p>\n<p><b>Example:</b></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>10</pre>\n<p>Output:</p>\n<pre>2\n4\n6\n8\n10</pre>",
