   "xml_index": 20,
   "xml_name": "L02_020_Multiplication Table",
   "display_name": "Multiplication Table",
   "questiontext_html": "<p>Time for the grand finale of Lab 2! Let's write a program every one of us has done by hand in school: printing a <strong>multiplication table</strong>.</p>\n<p>Given a number <code>n</code>, we want to print its table from 1 to 10, in the exact format <code>n x i = result</code> (with no spaces around the <code>x</code> and <code>=</code> symbols), one line per multiplication.</p>\n<p>For example, if <code>n = 2</code>, the table looks like:</p>\n<pre>2x1=2\n2x2=4\n2x3=6\n2x4=8\n2x5=10\n2x6=12\n2x7=14\n2x8=16\n2x9=18\n2x10=20</pre>\n<p>You will need a <code>while</code> loop with a counter <code>i</code> going from 1 to 10, and inside the loop, use string concatenation (with <code>str()</code> to convert numbers to strings) to build and print each line in the exact required format.</p>\n<p><strong>Your task:</strong> Read a whole number <code>n</code> and print its multiplication table from 1 to 10, in the exact format shown above.</p>\n<p><strong>Example:</strong></p>\n<p>Input:</p>\n<pre>2</pre>\n<p>Output: (as shown above, 10 lines)</p>",
   "answerpreload": "",
